onfig/ref/object parsing and stable rejection of gitfile, bare, linked, reftable, partial or exotic layouts. Nine JSON examples parse, 29 primary-source URLs are recorded, topic audit passes, curator-spec validates 30 schemas and 93 vectors, git diff --check passes, and stored resource bytes match. No product/spec/schema/code/test/release or prior resource was edited by this run.\\nBoard validation checkpoint 2026-07-27 — task-board validate still reports the same 45 pre-existing board-wide issues already logged for this scope: 12 legacy EPIC-260712 broken dependency text entries, one unsupported STORY-260720-35dck7 container link, parent-status mismatches, and two unrelated orphan resources. The newly attached v3 outcome is referenced and byte-identical; no new task-scoped board defect was introduced.\\nV3 evidence revision 2026-07-27 — after the first attachment, ran a temporary Git 2.50.1 argv smoke for full-object and exact-tag fetch flows; both fixed refs resolved and FETCH_HEAD remained absent. Updated the existing v3 outcome resource (not a duplicate) to record this evidence. Current SHA-256 is eb2a219d61a7a53709e588c5abc026b5f0ef34e7f235944432795bcc8861b966; this supersedes the earlier f9332203 attachment hash.\\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260727-c7cf8a, pid=78266, exit=0)\\nFresh v3 review directive 2026-07-27: independently review TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v3.md against both prior verdicts and primary Git/OpenSSH documentation. Do not edit producer or product/spec/code resources. Confirm every previously accepted identity/audit/cache/output/status/signing/future-driver requirement remains intact. Verify the exact init/fetch argv options and ordering exist in the pinned Git family, suppress templates/tags/FETCH_HEAD/submodules/maintenance/commit graph/remote ref choice, and implement locked-OID plus exact-tag fallback without hidden helpers or writes. Verify protocol-v0 SSH wrapper invocation shape and every OpenSSH option actually closes system/user config, prompts, TTY, forwarding, proxy/jump/local commands/control sockets while preserving only Git protocol pipes and operator auth. Verify the deliberately narrow local non-bare/files-ref admission is internally consistent for SHA-1/SHA-256, config grammar, HEAD/packed refs, object inventory, pack parsing/recomputation, mutation races, and stable rejection of unsupported layouts. Challenge excessive implementation burden only if a simpler equally closed private-object approach is provable. Validate JSON and cited claims. Attach a new v3 verdict resource; set done only if implementation-ready, otherwise route to analysis with exact remaining defects.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-863275, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-863275)\\nIndependent external-build-repository architecture v3 verdict: changes requested. Exact Git init/fetch and SSH isolation now pass review, but the packet remains non-implementable in three bounded areas: network raw-object helpers contradict the exact child graph and lack fixed vectors; local pack/index support is implementation-dependent across managers; and Git LFS pointer rejection is asserted without a normative detector. Full evidence is attached in TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-review-v3.md. Route to analysis, then a fresh reviewer cycle.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260727-863275, pid=5771, exit=0)\\nArchitecture v4 rework directive 2026-07-27: consume TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-review-v3.md and produce a new complete superseding TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v4.md. Preserve every accepted v3 section. Close the final three findings with one coherent design: add exact trusted read-only Git plumbing to the permitted child graph for both manager-owned network repositories and inert-copied local object stores, preferably one fixed cat-file --batch contract with absolute argv, clean environment, no replace/lazy fetch/optional locks/network/filters/textconv/mailmap, full-OID-only request grammar, byte-exact response grammar, bounded object count/size/depth/diagnostics, and manager parsing/recomputation of commit/tag/tree/blob IDs before audit; remove ambiguous ls-tree alternatives. Define one interoperable local packed-object admission contract, such as exact pack versions 2/3 and index version 2 with SHA-1/SHA-256 checksum/trailer rules, or an even narrower safe common subset; private config/object store must be manager-generated and source config never executed. Define an exact all-blob Git LFS pointer detector from the official pointer spec, including scan scope, size/line/extension/oid/size grammar, canonical/noncanonical policy, and stable build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported failure before audit; hydration remains forbidden. Validate exact argv with pinned Git, JSON, and primary sources. Do not edit product/spec/code or prior resources. Attach the new v4 resource and route to to-review.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-54d582, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-54d582)\ncreated:2026-07-20T01:44:31Z\nupdated:2026-07-27T19:11:00Z\nisBlocked:false\nisAdviso