15491-- FIX (R2): `runGo` dereferenced `command.ProcessState` on any `Run` error, but it is nil when process creation fails. Now nil-safe: a refusal sets `StartFailed`, `ExitCode = -1`, and the parent classifies it as the existing `go_list_failed`/`go_build_failed`. `Started` is documented as "times the single permitted creation site was used", so a refused attempt still consumes one and the exact-count process-graph guard is unchanged. A launcher identity failure now ends the session with its own stable code instead of a result with `Started == 0` that the parent misreported as a graph violation.
15492-- FINDING: a real, portable injection for the nil-`ProcessState` path is a manager-owned working directory that is inside the frozen snapshot but does not exist — the OS refuses `chdir` on both macOS and Windows and leaves no process state. On Windows the Job Object `ActiveProcessLimit = 1` additionally drives the same refusal through a complete `Build`, which is the closest thing to the scenario the review described.
15493-- ANOMALY: `cmd … & echo %ERRORLEVEL%` over ssh expands at parse time and always printed `0`. Every Windows gate reading taken that way was discarded and re-run with runtime `&& echo EXIT_0 || echo EXIT_NONZERO`. Related: `set VAR=1 && …` in `cmd.exe` keeps the trailing space, so `CURATOR_REAL_GO_BUILD_TEST` was `"1 "` and the real-build test silently skipped; the quoted `set "VAR=1"` form fixes it. Both are traps for any future native Windows evidence run.
