15501-- FINDING: teardown order matters. The process group must be killed **before** `cmd.Wait()` reaps the worker; after reaping, the pid is reusable and `kill(-pid)` could hit an unrelated group. `workerclient.go` drains the response pipe to EOF (worker exit closes it without reaping), then kills, then waits.
15502-- FIX: `filepath.IsAbs("/etc/passwd")` is false on Windows, so a rooted toolchain symlink was classified `toolchain_link_dangling` instead of `toolchain_link_absolute`. Added explicit leading `/` and `\` checks. `fingerprint.go:83`. First native Windows run of this package exposed it.
15503-- FINDING: Go's `os/exec` on Windows always installs `PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST` (`syscall/exec_windows.go:374`), so the inventory's `explicit-handle-inheritance-list` mechanism is what the standard library already does — the worker only has to add no handle.
