118:### 1606 — Withdrawn build-cache entries are never collected by the ordinary sweep, and `Revert`'s doc comment says they are
119-
120-- FINDING: `internal/buildcache/publish.go:366` documents on `Revert` that "the withdrawn entry is quarantined exactly like any other unusable one and is collected by the ordinary sweep". `Sweep` does not collect it.
121-- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/buildcache/collect.go:133` classifies cache-root members three ways — `entryNameRE` (`^[0-9a-f]{64}$`, `collect.go:31`), `sweepPrefix` (`".sweep-"`, `collect.go:29`), and `default`. `quarantinePrefix` is `".quarantine-"` (`publish.go:156`) and matches neither, so every withdrawn entry falls to `default`, is warned about as an *unrecognized cache root member* (`collect.go:148`), and is retained forever. Each `gc` re-emits the warning.
122-- FINDING: unguarded today. No test asserts the sweep's treatment of `.quarantine-*`, and the corrupt-repair and untrusted-repair paths both withdraw entries, so a long-lived manager home accumulates them silently.
123-- DECISION: ROUTED, not fixed. `TASK-260720-jrrgw9` is test-focused; the defect belongs to the owning build-cache implementation task. Fix is either teaching `Sweep` to collect `quarantinePrefix` members under the same grace rule, or correcting the `Revert` doc comment and documenting an operator reclaim path — plus a regression test for whichever is chosen.
124-- SCOPE: observed while reworking `cmd/curator/status_test.go` onto one shared compiled fixture. Because the cache root is now shared across cases, the rollback assertion `quarantinedEntries(t, home) != 1` became a delta against a baseline sampled before the failing run; the claim ("exactly the one this run published") is unchanged.
125-- STATUS: pending — needs an owning implementation task.
